Kasuga no Kami ([[:ja:春日神|春日神]]) also known as Kasuga Gongen ([[:ja:春日権現|春日権現]]) or Kasuga Daimyojin (春日大明神) is a god of {{ill|Kasuga Taisha|en|4=simple|5=User:Immanuelle/Kasuga-taisha}}.<ref name=":3">{{Cite book|title=The protocol of the gods: a study of the Kasuga cult in Japanese history|author=Grapard, Allan G.|date=1992|publisher=University of California Press|isbn=0520070976|oclc=25873140}}</ref><ref name=":4">{{Cite book|title=The miracles of the Kasuga deity|last=Tyler|first=Royall|date=2016|publisher=Columbia University Press|isbn=9780231534765|oclc=954193203}}</ref> It is composed of five separate deities each with a Shinto and a Buddhist equivalent.<ref name=":5" />

