The {{ill|Kasuga Gongen Genki|ja|春日権現験記}} stated that those studying {{ill|Yogācāra|ja|唯識論}} in the {{ill|Hossō sect|ja|法相宗}} were protected by Kasuga Gongen. The creation of {{ill|Kasuga Mandalas|ja|春日曼荼羅}} also flourished, depicting the honji-butsu of the main halls (First to Fourth Halls) and subsidiary shrines like Wakamiya.

