=== Tōhoku Region ===
* Kasuga Shrine (Rifu) ({{ill|Miyagi Prefecture|ja|宮城県}}, {{ill|Rifu|ja|利府町}})
* Kasuga Shrine (Tsuruoka) ({{ill|Yamagata Prefecture|ja|山形県}}, {{ill|Tsuruoka|ja|鶴岡市}}, Kushibiki Town) - Former prefectural shrine. {{ill|Kurokawa nō|ja|黒川能}} is designated as an {{ill|Important Intangible Folk Cultural Property|ja|重要無形民俗文化財}}.

=== Chūbu Region ===
* Kasuga Shrine (Joetsu) ({{ill|Niigata Prefecture|ja|新潟県}}, {{ill|Joetsu|ja|上越市}}, Kasuga) - Mentioned in the records of Kasuga Taisha as the first Kasuga Shrine in Japan, the namesake of {{ill|Kasugayama Castle|ja|春日山城}}.
* Kasuga Shrine (Sabae) ({{ill|Fukui Prefecture|ja|福井県}}, {{ill|Sabae|ja|鯖江市}}, Toriicho) - Main hall designated as an Important Cultural Property.
* {{ill|Kasuga Shrine (Seki)|ja|春日神社 (関市)}} ({{ill|Gifu Prefecture|ja|岐阜県}}, {{ill|Seki|ja|関市}}) - Festival costumes (63 items) designated as Important Cultural Properties.

=== Kinki Region ===
* {{ill|Kuwana Sōsha|ja|桑名宗社}} ({{ill|Mie Prefecture|ja|三重県}}, {{ill|Kuwana|ja|桑名市}}) - {{ill|Ishidori Matsuri|ja|石取祭}} is designated as an Important Intangible Folk Cultural Property.
* Kasuga Shrine (Ōtsu) ({{ill|Shiga Prefecture|ja|滋賀県}}, {{ill|Ōtsu|ja|大津市}}, Ōishi-Tomigawa) - Main hall designated as an Important Cultural Property.
* Kasuga Shrine (Yasu) (Shiga Prefecture, {{ill|Yasu|ja|野洲市}}) - Shrine gate designated as an Important Cultural Property.
* Kasuga Shrine (Rittō) (Shiga Prefecture, {{ill|Rittō|ja|栗東市}}) - Front gate designated as an Important Cultural Property.
* Kasuga Shrine (Higashiōmi) (Shiga Prefecture, {{ill|Higashiōmi|ja|東近江市}}, Koyagi Town) - Main hall designated as an Important Cultural Property.
* {{ill|Ōharano Shrine|ja|大原野神社}} ({{ill|Kyoto Prefecture|ja|京都府}}, {{ill|Kyoto|ja|京都市}}) - Former {{ill|Imperial shrine|ja|官幣中社}}, established near {{ill|Nagaokakyō|ja|長岡京}}. Also known as "Kyō Kasuga."
* {{ill|Yoshida Shrine|ja|吉田神社}} (Kyoto Prefecture, Kyoto City) - Former Imperial shrine. Enshrined Kasuga deities near {{ill|Heian-kyō|ja|平安京}}.
* Kasuga Shrine (Nantan) (Kyoto Prefecture, {{ill|Nantan|ja|南丹市}}, Sonobe Town, Takaya) - Main hall designated as an Important Cultural Property.
* Kasuga Shrine (Seika) (Kyoto Prefecture, {{ill|Seika|ja|精華町}}, Hishida-Miyakawara) - Main hall designated as an Important Cultural Property.
* {{ill|Hiraoka Shrine|ja|枚岡神社}} ({{ill|Osaka Prefecture|ja|大阪府}}, {{ill|Higashiōsaka|ja|東大阪市}}) - {{ill|Ichinomiya|ja|一宮|1=Ichinomiya}} of Kawachi Province, former Imperial shrine. Source of the deities {{ill|Ame-no-Koyane|ja|天児屋根大神}} and {{ill|Himegami|ja|比売大神|lt=Hime-no-Ōkami|1=Himegami|3=比売神}} for Kasuga Taisha. Also known as "Moto Kasuga."
* {{ill|Baiga Kasuga Shrine|ja|倍賀春日神社}} (Osaka Prefecture, {{ill|Ibaraki|ja|茨木市}}) - Kamakura-period stone lantern designated as an Important Cultural Property.
* {{ill|Kasuga Shrine (Tamba-Sasayama)|ja|春日神社 (丹波篠山市)}} ({{ill|Hyōgo Prefecture|ja|兵庫県}}, {{ill|Tamba-Sasayama|ja|丹波篠山市}}) - Former prefectural shrine. Noh stage designated as an Important Cultural Property.
* Kasuga Shrine (Yamatokōriyama) (Nara Prefecture, {{ill|Yamatokōriyama|ja|大和郡山市}}, Yada Town) - Located in the precincts of {{ill|Kongōzanji|ja|金剛山寺}}, main hall designated as an Important Cultural Property.
* Kasuga Shrine (Gojō) (Nara Prefecture, {{ill|Gojō|ja|五條市}}, Nishiyoshino Town, Mukai-Kanau) - Main hall designated as an Important Cultural Property.
* {{ill|Kada Kasuga Shrine|ja|加太春日神社}} ({{ill|Wakayama Prefecture|ja|和歌山県}}, {{ill|Wakayama|ja|和歌山市}}) - Main hall designated as an Important Cultural Property.

=== Chūgoku Region ===
* Kasuga Shrine (Okayama City, Kita Ward) ({{ill|Okayama Prefecture|ja|岡山県}}, {{ill|Okayama|ja|岡山市}}, {{ill|Kita-ku (Okayama)|ja|北区}}) - Former prefectural shrine.
* Kasuga Shrine (Hagi) ({{ill|Yamaguchi Prefecture|ja|山口県}}, {{ill|Hagi|ja|萩市}}) - Former prefectural shrine.

=== Shikoku Region ===
* {{ill|Kasuga Shrine (Tokushima)|ja|春日神社 (徳島市)}} ({{ill|Tokushima Prefecture|ja|徳島県}}, {{ill|Tokushima|ja|徳島市}}) - Former prefectural shrine.

=== Kyūshū Region ===
* {{ill|Kasuga Shrine (Kitakyūshū)|ja|春日神社 (北九州市)}} ({{ill|Fukuoka Prefecture|ja|福岡県}}, {{ill|Kitakyūshū|ja|北九州市}}) - Former prefectural shrine.
* {{ill|Kasuga Shrine (Kasuga)|ja|春日神社 (春日市)}} (Fukuoka Prefecture, {{ill|Kasuga|ja|春日市}}) - Known for "Kasuga no Mukooshi," designated as an Important Intangible Folk Cultural Property.
* {{ill|Kasuga Shrine (Ōita)|ja|春日神社 (大分市)|1=Kasuga Shrine (Ōita)}} ({{ill|Ōita Prefecture|ja|大分県}}, {{ill|Ōita|ja|大分市}}) - Former prefectural shrine, {{ill|Beppyo Shrine|ja|別表神社}}.

== Syncretism ==
{{see also|Kasuga Gongen}}
Under the {{ill|honji suijaku|ja|本地垂迹}} framework, the Kasuga deity (Kasuga Myōjin) was identified with {{ill|Amoghapasha|ja|不空羂索観音|fr|Amoghapasha Lokeshvara |id|Arca Amoghapasa|jv|Arca Amoghapasa|zh|不空羂索觀音|simple|User:Immanuelle/Amoghapasha}}, an incarnation of {{ill|Kannon|ja|観音菩薩}}.<ref>羽田守快『あなたを幸せにみちびく　観音さま』大法輪閣、2014th year 、p.112.</ref>

== In Popular culture ==
Kasuga-no-Kami, Jade Angel is a card in {{ill|WIXOSS|en|4=ja}}.

